<http://data.silknow.org/object/fe92160e-261b-3c52-b490-76a5b51a68a8>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Imperial dragon robe, silk tapestry weave (<i>kesi</i>), China, Qing dynasty, 1780-1850."@en , "Chinese Imperial dragon robe of silk tapestry weave (<i>kesi</i>). Yellow and blue ground. Sky, earth and water, 9 large 5-clawed dragons pursuing and clasping sacred discs among clouds, bats, the 12 symbols and symbols of longevity (worked in red, pink, blue, yellow and white silks and gold thread) on a yellow and blue fret background. Collar and cuffs of similar design with fret background. Lined with yellow satin."@en ;
